      "fix": "Under prefers-reduced-motion draw single still frames (one per beat), turn off parallax, scrubbing, smooth-scroll and looping CSS animation, and keep short fades only."
    },
    {
      "points": 10,
      "ok": true,
      "name": "Little script before first paint",
      "detail": "133 KB of script requested before first paint (budget 170 KB); 157 KB in all",
      "fix": "Load the 3D engine with a dynamic import() after first paint (or when the scene is near the viewport). Keep the heading as real text so it paints first."
    },
    {
      "points": 10,
      "ok": true,
      "name": "Page weight",
      "detail": "157 KB total (script 133, images 0, 3D assets 0, fonts 0); biggest: 133 KB three.min.js; 24 KB index.html",
      "fix": "Budget: first scene under about 1.5 MB on phones and 4 MB on desktop. Compress models (meshopt or Draco) and textures (KTX2 / WebP), cut texture size, lazy-load what is below the fold."
    },
    {
      "points": 5,
      "ok": true,
      "name": "Phone: pixel ratio is capped",
      "detail": "canvas draws at 1.92x on a 3x screen, 1.0 megapixels",
      "fix": "Cap the pixel ratio at 1.5 on touch screens (2 at most) and lower it when frames get slow. A 3x canvas draws 9 pixels for every CSS pixel."
    },
    {
      "points": 5,
      "ok": true,
      "name": "Phone: no sideways scroll",
      "detail": "fits 390px",
      "fix": "Give the scene host overflow: hidden and min-width: 0; size the canvas from its box, not from the window."
    },
    {
      "points": 10,
      "ok": true,
      "name": "Scrolling stays native",
      "detail": "page does not scroll",
      "fix": "Never change scroll speed or direction and never replace the scrollbar with a transform. Pin with position: sticky and read the scroll position; let the browser do the scrolling."
    },
    {
      "points": 5,
      "ok": null,
      "name": "Scene pauses off screen",
      "detail": "the canvas is always on screen (or there is none)",
      "fix": "Stop the render loop with an IntersectionObserver when the scene leaves the viewport, and on visibilitychange when the tab is hidden."
    },
    {
      "points": 5,
      "ok": true,
      "name": "Ambient motion rests or can be paused",
      "detail": "62.7 frames/s still being drawn about 7s after load with no input; a pause control was found",
      "fix": "Anything that moves by itself for more than 5 seconds needs a visible pause control (WCAG 2.2.2), or should settle and render on demand."
    },
    {
      "points": 5,
      "ok": true,
      "name": "Survives a lost graphics context",
      "detail": "0 error(s) after the context was lost; webglcontextlost handler present",
      "fix": "Listen for webglcontextlost (preventDefault, stop the loop, show the fallback) and rebuild on webglcontextrestored. Phones drop contexts when memory is tight."
    }
